import ../../site/programs/controller.dl
import site_fixture.dl

to wake recorded website view {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    ignore view

set driver to a website shader test driver
set driver's wake to (the function named "wake recorded website view $") as a pointer
set instance to an instance of website fixture
set view to a new UI view
set view's driver to the address of driver
set view's instance to the address of instance
set view's active to true
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set state's shader editor's description to the custom website shader
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
set still to a new website shader view
set still's resource to 1 as a pointer
set still's program to a JSON object containing [JSON child "passes" is (a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON child "uniforms" is (a new JSON-RPC array)]])]
set view's seconds to 1.0
advance website shader (the address of still) visible true in (the address of view)
set view's seconds to 2.0
advance website shader (the address of still) visible true in (the address of view)
require condition (still's seconds = 0.0) reporting "A shader without a time input kept animating"
free still's program
select website editor mode 1 in (the address of state)
set the text of "IDE output" in (the address of instance) to "Retained program output"
run website program 2 in (the address of state)
require condition ((the item at 2 in (state's programs))'s phase = 1) reporting "The shader did not start compiling"
set stage to a JSON object containing [JSON text "webgpu" is "code", JSON text "webgl" is "code", JSON child "resources" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "glslBindings" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "glslUniforms" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "vertexInputs" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "uniforms" is (a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "name" is "time", JSON number "group" is 0, JSON number "binding" is 0, JSON child "type" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "scalar" is "float32", JSON number "rows" is 1, JSON number "columns" is 1])]])]
set response to a JSON object containing [JSON number "status" is 0, JSON number "milliseconds" is 1.5, JSON child "stages" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "fragment" is stage])]
receive website compilation response for 2 in (the address of state)
free response
require condition ((the item at 2 in (state's programs))'s phase = 2) reporting "A shader build did not create its graphics program"
set response to a JSON object containing [JSON number "resource" is 42, JSON number "passes" is 1]
receive the website shader preview response in (the address of state)
free response
set rendering to the address of (state's shader editor's preview)
require condition ((the item at 2 in (state's programs))'s phase = 3) reporting "A linked shader did not become a running preview"
set view's seconds to 10.0
advance website shader rendering visible true in (the address of view)
set view's seconds to 10.25
advance website shader rendering visible true in (the address of view)
require condition (rendering's seconds = 0.25) reporting "The preview clock did not advance by the frame time"
set view's seconds to 11.0
advance website shader rendering visible false in (the address of view)
set view's seconds to 30.0
advance website shader rendering visible true in (the address of view)
require condition (rendering's seconds = 0.25) reporting "Returning to a preview counted time spent offscreen"
set view's active to false
set view's seconds to 31.0
advance website shader rendering visible true in (the address of view)
require condition (rendering's active = false) reporting "An inactive surface kept its shader clock active"
set view's active to true
set view's seconds to 60.0
advance website shader rendering visible true in (the address of view)
require condition (rendering's seconds = 0.25) reporting "Returning to the tab counted time spent inactive"
stop website program 2 in (the address of state)
require condition (rendering's paused) reporting "Stop did not pause the preview"
toggle the website shader preview in (the address of state)
require condition (rendering's paused = false) reporting "A paused preview could not resume"
reset the website shader preview in (the address of state)
require condition (rendering's seconds = 0.0) reporting "Reset did not restart the preview clock"
ignore the rendered website shader rendering sized 320 by 180 in (the address of view)
ignore the rendered website shader rendering sized 320 by 180 in (the address of view)
set rendering's seconds to 0.5
ignore the rendered website shader rendering sized 320 by 180 in (the address of view)
ignore the rendered website shader rendering sized 321 by 180 in (the address of view)
run website program 2 in (the address of state)
toggle the website shader preview in (the address of state)
require condition ((the item at 2 in (state's programs))'s phase = 1) reporting "Preview playback interrupted an in-flight compilation"
set response to a JSON object containing [JSON number "status" is 1, JSON number "milliseconds" is 1, JSON child "diagnostics" is (a new JSON-RPC array)]
receive website compilation response for 2 in (the address of state)
free response
require condition (rendering's resource = (42 as a pointer)) reporting "A failed edit discarded the last successful preview"
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "IDE output" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "Retained program output") reporting "Shader editing discarded the program tab's output"
run website program 2 in (the address of state)
set stage to a JSON object containing [JSON text "webgpu" is "new code", JSON text "webgl" is "new code", JSON child "resources" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "glslBindings" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "glslUniforms" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "vertexInputs" is (a new JSON-RPC array), JSON child "uniforms" is (a new JSON-RPC array)]
set response to a JSON object containing [JSON number "status" is 0, JSON number "milliseconds" is 1, JSON child "stages" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "fragment" is stage])]
receive website compilation response for 2 in (the address of state)
free response
toggle the website shader preview in (the address of state)
require condition ((the item at 2 in (state's programs))'s phase = 2) reporting "Preview playback interrupted graphics creation"
stop website program 2 in (the address of state)
set response to a JSON object containing [JSON number "resource" is 43]
discard website reply response for purpose 10 in (the address of state)
free response
require condition (state's shader editor's pending program = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to JSON value)) reporting "A cancelled graphics request retained its description"
free rendering's program
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close the address of instance
print line "Shader compilation, last-successful previews, playback and cancellation share DynLex state."
